    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0218" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg206"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1956: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-03T16:00:00+03:25">December 3, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 3—3:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>412. Political situation continues to drift hopelessly. Relations between Majlis
                    and Government unimproved, most deputies continuing to play their game of
                    obstruction and opportunism. For example Budget Bill for year now nearing end
                    not yet passed. The Full Powers Bill was referred to committee without mention
                    of urgency.</p>
                <pb facs="0219" n="207" xml:id="pg207"/>
                <p>Political intrigue against Qavam<anchor n="77" xml:id="d220-f1"/> is increasing;
                    leading candidates being mentioned are Soheily<anchor n="78" xml:id="d220-f2"/>
                    and Ali Mansour. Cabinet changes are imminent, principal one being dismissal of
                    Gharagozlou as Minister of Justice.</p>
                <p>It seems likely the rapidly developing food shortage will bring about new crisis
                    which will result in Qavam’s fall or dissolution of Majlis. There can be no
                    continuity or stability in Government as long as Majlis is composed of
                    irresponsible elements intent on pursuing their own interests.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d220-f1" n="77" xml:id="d220-f1-content">
                <p>Ahmad Qavam, Prime Minister of Iran.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d220-f2" n="78" xml:id="d220-f2-content">
                <p>Ali Soheily, former Prime Minister of Iran.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
